{"formatVersion":1,"translationId":"BSB","textDirection":"ltr","bookId":"NAM","bookName":"Nahum","chapters":[{"number":1,"lastVerse":15,"verses":[{"number":1,"lines":[{"text":"This is the burden against Nineveh, the book of the vision of Nahum the Elkoshite:"}]},{"number":2,"lines":[{"text":"The LORD is a jealous and avenging God;","poem":1},{"text":"the LORD is avenging and full of wrath.","poem":2},{"text":"The LORD takes vengeance on His foes","poem":1},{"text":"and reserves wrath for His enemies.","poem":2}]},{"number":3,"lines":[{"text":"The LORD is slow to anger","poem":1},{"text":"and great in power;","poem":2},{"text":"the LORD will by no means","poem":1},{"text":"leave the guilty unpunished.","poem":2},{"text":"His path is in the whirlwind and storm,","poem":1},{"text":"and clouds are the dust beneath His feet.","poem":2}]},{"number":4,"lines":[{"text":"He rebukes the sea and dries it up;","poem":1},{"text":"He makes all the rivers run dry.","poem":2},{"text":"Bashan and Carmel wither,","poem":1},{"text":"and the flower of Lebanon wilts.","poem":2}]},{"number":5,"lines":[{"text":"The mountains quake before Him,","poem":1},{"text":"and the hills melt away;","poem":2},{"text":"the earth trembles at His presence—","poem":1},{"text":"the world and all its dwellers.","poem":2}]},{"number":6,"lines":[{"text":"Who can withstand His indignation?","poem":1},{"text":"Who can endure His burning anger?","poem":2},{"text":"His wrath is poured out like fire;","poem":1},{"text":"even rocks are shattered before Him.","poem":2}]},{"number":7,"lines":[{"text":"The LORD is good,","poem":1},{"text":"a stronghold in the day of distress;","poem":2},{"text":"He cares for those who trust in Him.","poem":2}]},{"number":8,"lines":[{"text":"But with an overwhelming flood","poem":1},{"text":"He will make an end of Nineveh","poem":2},{"text":"and pursue His enemies into darkness.","poem":2}]},{"number":9,"lines":[{"text":"Whatever you plot against the LORD,","poem":1},{"text":"He will bring to an end.","poem":2},{"text":"Affliction will not rise up","poem":1},{"text":"a second time.","poem":2}]},{"number":10,"lines":[{"text":"For they will be entangled as with thorns","poem":1},{"text":"and consumed like the drink of a drunkard—","poem":2},{"text":"like stubble that is fully dry.","poem":2}]},{"number":11,"lines":[{"text":"From you, O Nineveh, comes forth","poem":1},{"text":"a plotter of evil against the LORD,","poem":2},{"text":"a counselor of wickedness.","poem":2}]},{"number":12,"lines":[{"text":"This is what the LORD says:"},{"text":"“Though they are allied and numerous,","poem":1},{"text":"yet they will be cut down and pass away.","poem":2},{"text":"Though I have afflicted you, O Judah,","poem":1},{"text":"I will afflict you no longer.","poem":2}]},{"number":13,"lines":[{"text":"For I will now break their yoke from your neck","poem":1},{"text":"and tear away your shackles.”","poem":2}]},{"number":14,"lines":[{"text":"The LORD has issued a command concerning you, O Nineveh:"},{"text":"“There will be no descendants","poem":1},{"text":"to carry on your name.","poem":2},{"text":"I will cut off the carved image and cast idol","poem":1},{"text":"from the house of your gods;","poem":2},{"text":"I will prepare your grave,","poem":1},{"text":"for you are contemptible.”","poem":2}]},{"number":15,"lines":[{"text":"Look to the mountains—","poem":1},{"text":"the feet of one who brings good news,","poem":2},{"text":"who proclaims peace!","poem":2},{"text":"Celebrate your feasts, O Judah;","poem":1},{"text":"fulfill your vows.","poem":2},{"text":"For the wicked will never again march through you;","poem":1},{"text":"they will be utterly cut off.","poem":2}]}]},{"number":2,"lastVerse":13,"verses":[{"number":1,"lines":[{"text":"One who scatters advances","poem":1},{"text":"against you, O Nineveh.","poem":2},{"text":"Guard the fortress!","poem":1},{"text":"Watch the road!","poem":2},{"text":"Brace yourselves!","poem":1},{"text":"Summon all your strength!","poem":2}]},{"number":2,"lines":[{"text":"For the LORD will restore the splendor of Jacob","poem":1},{"text":"like the splendor of Israel,","poem":2},{"text":"though destroyers have laid them waste","poem":1},{"text":"and ruined the branches of their vine.","poem":2}]},{"number":3,"lines":[{"text":"The shields of his mighty men are red;","poem":1},{"text":"the valiant warriors are dressed in scarlet.","poem":2},{"text":"The fittings of the chariots flash like fire","poem":1},{"text":"on the day they are prepared,","poem":2},{"text":"and the spears of cypress","poem":1},{"text":"have been brandished.","poem":2}]},{"number":4,"lines":[{"text":"The chariots dash through the streets;","poem":1},{"text":"they rush around the plazas,","poem":2},{"text":"appearing like torches,","poem":1},{"text":"darting about like lightning.","poem":2}]},{"number":5,"lines":[{"text":"He summons his nobles;","poem":1},{"text":"they stumble as they advance.","poem":2},{"text":"They race to its wall;","poem":1},{"text":"the protective shield is set in place.","poem":2}]},{"number":6,"lines":[{"text":"The river gates are thrown open","poem":1},{"text":"and the palace collapses.","poem":2}]},{"number":7,"lines":[{"text":"It is decreed that the city be exiled","poem":1},{"text":"and carried away;","poem":2},{"text":"her maidservants moan like doves,","poem":1},{"text":"and beat upon their breasts.","poem":2}]},{"number":8,"lines":[{"text":"Nineveh has been like a pool of water","poem":1},{"text":"throughout her days,","poem":2},{"text":"but now it is draining away.","poem":2},{"text":"“Stop! Stop!” they cry,","poem":1},{"text":"but no one turns back.","poem":2}]},{"number":9,"lines":[{"text":"“Plunder the silver!","poem":1},{"text":"Plunder the gold!”","poem":2},{"text":"There is no end to the treasure,","poem":1},{"text":"an abundance of every precious thing.","poem":2}]},{"number":10,"lines":[{"text":"She is emptied!","poem":1},{"text":"Yes, she is desolate and laid waste!","poem":2},{"text":"Hearts melt, knees knock,","poem":1},{"text":"bodies tremble, and every face grows pale!","poem":2}]},{"number":11,"lines":[{"text":"Where is the lions’ lair","poem":1},{"text":"or the feeding ground of the young lions,","poem":2},{"text":"where the lion and lioness prowled with their cubs,","poem":1},{"text":"with nothing to frighten them away?","poem":2}]},{"number":12,"lines":[{"text":"The lion mauled enough for its cubs","poem":1},{"text":"and strangled prey for the lioness.","poem":2},{"text":"It filled its dens with the kill,","poem":1},{"text":"and its lairs with mauled prey.","poem":2}]},{"number":13,"lines":[{"text":"“Behold, I am against you,”","poem":1},{"text":"declares the LORD of Hosts.","poem":2},{"text":"“I will reduce your chariots to cinders,","poem":1},{"text":"and the sword will devour your young lions.","poem":2},{"text":"I will cut off your prey from the earth,","poem":1},{"text":"and the voices of your messengers","poem":2},{"text":"will no longer be heard.”","poem":2}]}]},{"number":3,"lastVerse":19,"verses":[{"number":1,"lines":[{"text":"Woe to the city of blood,","poem":1},{"text":"full of lies,","poem":2},{"text":"full of plunder,","poem":1},{"text":"never without prey.","poem":2}]},{"number":2,"lines":[{"text":"The crack of the whip,","poem":1},{"text":"the rumble of the wheel,","poem":2},{"text":"galloping horse","poem":1},{"text":"and bounding chariot!","poem":2}]},{"number":3,"lines":[{"text":"Charging horseman,","poem":1},{"text":"flashing sword,","poem":2},{"text":"shining spear;","poem":2},{"text":"heaps of slain,","poem":1},{"text":"mounds of corpses,","poem":2},{"text":"dead bodies without end—","poem":1},{"text":"they stumble over their dead—","poem":2}]},{"number":4,"lines":[{"text":"because of the many harlotries of the harlot,","poem":1},{"text":"the seductive mistress of sorcery,","poem":2},{"text":"who betrays nations by her prostitution","poem":1},{"text":"and clans by her witchcraft.","poem":2}]},{"number":5,"lines":[{"text":"“Behold, I am against you,”","poem":1},{"text":"declares the LORD of Hosts.","poem":2},{"text":"“I will lift your skirts over your face.","poem":1},{"text":"I will show your nakedness to the nations","poem":2},{"text":"and your shame to the kingdoms.","poem":2}]},{"number":6,"lines":[{"text":"I will pelt you with filth","poem":1},{"text":"and treat you with contempt;","poem":2},{"text":"I will make a spectacle of you.","poem":2}]},{"number":7,"lines":[{"text":"Then all who see you","poem":1},{"text":"will recoil from you and say,","poem":2},{"text":"‘Nineveh is devastated;","poem":1},{"text":"who will grieve for her?’","poem":2},{"text":"Where can I find","poem":1},{"text":"comforters for you?”","poem":2}]},{"number":8,"lines":[{"text":"Are you better than Thebes,","poem":1},{"text":"stationed by the Nile with water around her,","poem":2},{"text":"whose rampart was the sea,","poem":1},{"text":"whose wall was the water?","poem":2}]},{"number":9,"lines":[{"text":"Cush and Egypt were her boundless strength;","poem":1},{"text":"Put and Libya were her allies.","poem":2}]},{"number":10,"lines":[{"text":"Yet she became an exile;","poem":1},{"text":"she went into captivity.","poem":2},{"text":"Her infants were dashed to pieces","poem":1},{"text":"at the head of every street.","poem":2},{"text":"They cast lots for her dignitaries,","poem":1},{"text":"and all her nobles were bound in chains.","poem":2}]},{"number":11,"lines":[{"text":"You too will become drunk;","poem":1},{"text":"you will go into hiding","poem":2},{"text":"and seek refuge from the enemy.","poem":2}]},{"number":12,"lines":[{"text":"All your fortresses are fig trees","poem":1},{"text":"with the first ripe figs;","poem":2},{"text":"when shaken, they fall","poem":1},{"text":"into the mouth of the eater!","poem":2}]},{"number":13,"lines":[{"text":"Look at your troops—","poem":1},{"text":"they are like your women!","poem":2},{"text":"The gates of your land","poem":1},{"text":"are wide open to your enemies;","poem":2},{"text":"fire consumes their bars.","poem":2}]},{"number":14,"lines":[{"text":"Draw your water for the siege;","poem":1},{"text":"strengthen your fortresses.","poem":2},{"text":"Work the clay and tread the mortar;","poem":1},{"text":"repair the brick kiln!","poem":2}]},{"number":15,"lines":[{"text":"There the fire will devour you;","poem":1},{"text":"the sword will cut you down","poem":2},{"text":"and consume you like a young locust.","poem":2},{"text":"Make yourself many like the young locust;","poem":1},{"text":"make yourself many like the swarming locust!","poem":2}]},{"number":16,"lines":[{"text":"You have multiplied your merchants","poem":1},{"text":"more than the stars of the sky.","poem":2},{"text":"The young locust strips the land","poem":1},{"text":"and flies away.","poem":2}]},{"number":17,"lines":[{"text":"Your guards are like the swarming locust,","poem":1},{"text":"and your scribes like clouds of locusts","poem":2},{"text":"that settle on the walls on a cold day.","poem":2},{"text":"When the sun rises, they fly away,","poem":1},{"text":"and no one knows where.","poem":2}]},{"number":18,"lines":[{"text":"O king of Assyria, your shepherds slumber;","poem":1},{"text":"your officers sleep.","poem":2},{"text":"Your people are scattered on the mountains","poem":1},{"text":"with no one to gather them.","poem":2}]},{"number":19,"lines":[{"text":"There is no healing for your injury;","poem":1},{"text":"your wound is severe.","poem":2},{"text":"All who hear the news of you","poem":1},{"text":"applaud your downfall,","poem":2},{"text":"for who has not experienced","poem":1},{"text":"your constant cruelty?","poem":2}]}]}]}
